    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5ac83aac_e6662936",
        "filename": "chip/ish/ipc_heci.c",
        "patchSetId": 19
      },
      "lineNbr": 660,
      "author": {
        "id": 1259838
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-12-05T23:16:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As I read through this again, I am realizing more.\n\nIs the intent to create a new task for every type of protocol (e.g. Management, HECI, etc) that can be transmitted on this doorbell interface? If so, then we will have multiple tasks reading from the same register set (and blocking each other if they are slow to read because they are processing the previous command or something).\n\nShould we create a rx_queue that buffers the raw data; That way, only a single task (and interrupt context) are accessing these registers. I think we would want a similar paradigm for TX, i.e. only a single task is access these host_ish registers. We already have the queue for it, so let\u0027s make a single task read/write to these registers.\n\nI still think having separate tasks to process the different protocols makes sense, they just read and write to the TX and RX buffers instead of directly to the doorbell registers themselves.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 660,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 660,
        "endChar": 17
      },
      "revId": "6d422a756645eea0e457f29ca549e521e3b3f1f9",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2e0fc4f2_3b2ba3da",
        "filename": "chip/ish/ipc_heci.c",
        "patchSetId": 19
      },
      "lineNbr": 660,
      "author": {
        "id": 1137654
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-12-06T00:37:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I got it. Actually the first version(still I have like below) kept one for each protocol for\n- not to block other protocol service\n- handle emergency msg.\nit makes sense because upper layer has its own flow control which is mostly (stop and wait). but I thought it\u0027s too much for sensor handling. but OK, as you wish, I\u0027ll come up with better one tomorrow.\n\nstruct ipc_msg_event {\n    uint8_t enabled;\n    task_id_t task_id;\n    uint32_t event;\n\n    struct ipc_msg last_msg; /* do we need validity flag for msg ? */\n};\n\n....\n\nstatic void ipc_interrupt_handler(void)\n{\n    struct ipc_if_ctx *ctx;\n    uint32_t pisr \u003d REG32(IPC_PISR);\n    uint32_t pimr \u003d REG32(IPC_PIMR);\n    uint32_t busy_clear \u003d REG32(IPC_BUSY_CLEAR);\n    uint32_t drbl_val, payload_size;\n    uint8_t protocol;\n\n    if ((pisr \u0026 IPC_PISR_HOST2ISH_BIT) \u0026\u0026 (pimr \u0026 IPC_PIMR_HOST2ISH_BIT)) {\n        ipc_clear_pimr_host_db();\n\n        ctx \u003d ipc_get_if_ctx(IPC_PEER_HOST_ID);\n        drbl_val \u003d REG32(ctx-\u003ein_drbl_reg);\n        protocol \u003d IPC_DB_PROTOCOL(drbl_val);\n        payload_size \u003d IPC_DB_MSG_LENGTH(drbl_val);\n\n        CPRINTF(\"!! int[d\u003d0x%0x, p\u003d%d !!\\n\", drbl_val, protocol );\n\n        /* send event */\n        if (ctx-\u003emsg_events[protocol].enabled) {\n            ctx-\u003emsg_events[protocol].last_msg.db_val \u003d drbl_val;\n            memcpy(ctx-\u003emsg_events[protocol].last_msg.payload,\n                   (void *)ctx-\u003ein_msg_reg, payload_size);\n\n            task_set_event(ctx-\u003emsg_events[protocol].task_id,\n                       ctx-\u003emsg_events[protocol].event, 0);\n        } else {\n            CPRINTS(\"discard msg and make ipc available\");\n            REG32(ctx-\u003ein_drbl_reg) \u003d 0;\n            ipc_set_pimr_host_db();\n            ipc_send_cmpl_indication(IPC_BUILD_HOST_MNG_HANDLE());\n        }\n    }\n\n    if ((busy_clear \u0026 IPC_DB_CLR_STS_ISH2HOST_BIT) \u0026\u0026\n        (pimr \u0026 IPC_PIMR_ISH2HOST_CLR_BIT)) {\n        ctx \u003d ipc_get_if_ctx(IPC_PEER_HOST_ID);\n        mutex_unlock(\u0026ctx-\u003ewrite_lock);\n\n        REG32(IPC_BUSY_CLEAR) \u003d ctx-\u003eclr_bit;\n    }\n}",
      "parentUuid": "5ac83aac_e6662936",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 660,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 660,
        "endChar": 17
      },
      "revId": "6d422a756645eea0e457f29ca549e521e3b3f1f9",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
