    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "62e796bc_f01c3fd8",
        "filename": "chip/ish/ipc_heci.c",
        "patchSetId": 19
      },
      "lineNbr": 660,
      "author": {
        "id": 1259838
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-12-11T21:38:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Let\u0027s drop this task structure discussion for now and keep the interface the way it currently is.\n\nI see issues in the what I was suggesting about task structure: if the RX queue for a protocol fills up quickly, then that protocol task will still block other protocol tasks from completing as long as the single doorbell register has a new message waiting for that blocking full protocol. \nI was also thinking that we could pull all of the incoming messages as fast as we could and let the ISH processes them as needed, but the host may be able to send messages much more quickly than the ISH can process (so we would end up in the full queue scenario often).",
      "parentUuid": "2e0fc4f2_3b2ba3da",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 660,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 660,
        "endChar": 17
      },
      "revId": "6d422a756645eea0e457f29ca549e521e3b3f1f9",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "22656b38_434824fd",
        "filename": "chip/ish/ipc_heci.c",
        "patchSetId": 19
      },
      "lineNbr": 660,
      "author": {
        "id": 1137654
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-12-12T01:31:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "by nature of IPC flow control\n- only one transaction(one meaningful message) per protocol from host can use IPC H/W at the same time.\n- if corresponding task reads the transaction, IPC H/W is free to others. There\u0027s no lock/unlock mechanism here but combination of how host send a transaction through IPC and IPC busy bit flow control makes this happens.\n- Host doesn\u0027t send any message until IPC busy bit clear. this is IPC level flow control.\n\nIt is more \"can there be more than one transaction for a protocol\"\n- one task received the transaction and busy with processing it. If we allow host to send another transaction then the task in processing the previous transaction should be able to read new transaction while processing it. Or we should maintain two tasks \"reading\" and \"processing\". \n\nBUT the thing is I don\u0027t think ISH will get two different transactions for one protocol. Host point of view, I believe it will be always \"send one\" and \"wait response\"(maybe with timeout).",
      "parentUuid": "62e796bc_f01c3fd8",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 660,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 660,
        "endChar": 17
      },
